    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is Shopify better than Squarespace for ecommerce?</h3>
    <p>Yes, Shopify is better for dedicated ecommerce because it is built specifically for online stores. Shopify includes unlimited products, a conversion-optimized checkout, inventory management, abandoned cart recovery, and over 8,000 commerce apps. Squarespace has ecommerce features but they are lighter, with product limits on lower plans and fewer payment gateway options. If your primary goal is selling products online, Shopify wins. If you want a beautiful website that also sells a few products, Squarespace is the better choice.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, Shopify or Squarespace?</h3>
    <p>Squarespace is cheaper at the entry level. The Business plan at $23 per month includes ecommerce with a 3% transaction fee, while the Commerce Basic plan at $27 per month removes the fee and adds unlimited products. Shopify Basic costs $29 per month with no transaction fees on Shopify Payments. For a small store with under 50 products, Squarespace Commerce Basic is slightly cheaper. For stores that need apps, multi-channel selling, or higher volume, Shopify offers better value despite the higher monthly fee.</p>

    <h3>Which has better design templates, Shopify or Squarespace?</h3>
    <p>Squarespace has better design templates for content-driven websites. Its templates are award-winning, visually striking, and ideal for portfolios, restaurants, and lifestyle brands. Shopify themes are optimized for conversion and product display rather than editorial beauty, with 12 free themes and over 100 paid themes. For a store where design and storytelling matter as much as sales, Squarespace wins on aesthetics. For a store where product conversion is the priority, Shopify themes are better tuned for sales.</p>

    <h3>Can I migrate from Squarespace to Shopify?</h3>
    <p>Yes, you can migrate from Squarespace to Shopify. Shopify offers a free Store Importer app that transfers products, customers, and order history directly from Squarespace. The process typically takes a few hours for stores under 200 products. You will need to manually redirect old URLs to preserve SEO, and some Squarespace page content like blog posts may need to be migrated separately. Many merchants rebuild their content pages in Shopify because the page editors work differently.</p>

    <h3>Which platform is better for SEO, Shopify or Squarespace?</h3>
    <p>Both platforms handle SEO basics well, including fast page loads, SSL, and editable meta tags. Shopify has a slight edge for ecommerce SEO because it includes built-in schema markup for products, faster checkout, and stronger multi-channel selling that drives traffic. Squarespace has excellent SEO for content sites with a strong blog engine and clean URLs. For product-heavy stores, Shopify wins. For content-driven sites that also sell products, Squarespace's blog engine is stronger out of the box.</p>

    <h3>Can I use Shopify and Squarespace together?</h3>
    <p>It is not practical to run both platforms for the same store, but some businesses use Squarespace for their main marketing website and Shopify for a separate store subdomain. A more common approach is to pick one platform based on whether your site is content-first or commerce-first. If 80% of your revenue comes from products, choose Shopify. If 80% comes from content, services, or bookings with a small product component, choose Squarespace Commerce. Most merchants choose one platform within the first month of a free trial.</p>

